י ( הֶבְלוֺ , הֶבְלְךָ ) הֶבְלִי Eccl 7:15 ; Eccl 9:9 , ׳ יְמֵי חַיֵּי ה Eccl 6:12 ; Eccl 9:9 ; Job 27:12 (see הָבַל ), Isa 49:4 לְתֹהוּ וָהֶבֶל for nought and vanity have I spent my strength; as adverb accusative vainly, to no purpose Isa 30:7 הֶבֶל וָרִיק יַעֲזֹ֑רוּ , Ps 39:7 אַךְ הֶבֶל יֶהֱמָיוּן they disquiet themselves to no purpose , Job 9:29 : הֶבֶל אִיגָָֽע Job 35:16 , with נִחַם to comfort Job 21:34 ; Zech 10:2 . Plural הֲבָלִים of false gods, Deut 32:21 ) כִּעֲסוּנִי בְהַבְלֵיהֶם || בְּלֹאאֵֿל ) 1Kgs 16:13 ; 1Kgs 16:26 ; Jer 8:19 הַבְלֵי נֵכָר || (בִּפְסִילֵיהֶםׅ , Jer 10:8 ; Jer 14:22 הַבְלֵי הַגּוֺיִם , Ps 31:7 הַשֹּׁמְרִים הַבְלֵישָֿׁוְא empty vanities Jonah 2:9 in more general sense Eccl 1:2 (twice in verse); Eccl 12:8 הֲבֵל הֲבָלִים , Eccl 5:6 .", "definition_html": "<h1><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB2041')\">BDB2041</entry> [<entry onclick=\"sn('H1892')\">H1892</entry>]</h1><div class=\"navigation\"><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB2040')\">BDB2040</entry> | BIBLICAL HEBREW | <entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB2042')\">BDB2042</entry></div><p> I. <bdbheb>הֶ֫בֶל</bdbheb><sub>73</sub> <b>noun masculine</b> <highlightword>vapour, breath</highlightword> (Late Hebrew <highlight>id.</highlight>, Syriac <placeholder1230/> <highlight>id.</highlight>) figurative vanity (so Late Hebrew, Syriac <placeholder1231/>) — <bdbheb>הָ֑בֶל</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Eccl 1:2\" b=\"21\" cBegin=\"1\" vBegin=\"2\" cEnd=\"1\" vEnd=\"2\" onclick=\"bcv(21,1,2)\">Eccl 1:2</ref> +; construct <bdbheb>הֲבֵל</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Eccl 1:2\" b=\"21\" cBegin=\"1\" vBegin=\"2\" cEnd=\"1\" vEnd=\"2\" onclick=\"bcv(21,1,2)\">Eccl 1:2</ref> (twice in verse); <ref ref=\"Eccl 12:8\" b=\"21\" cBegin=\"12\" vBegin=\"8\" cEnd=\"12\" vEnd=\"8\" onclick=\"bcv(21,12,8)\">Eccl 12:8</ref>, suffix <bdbheb>הֶבְלִי</bdbheb> etc. <ref ref=\"Eccl 6:12\" b=\"21\" cBegin=\"6\" vBegin=\"12\" cEnd=\"6\" vEnd=\"12\" onclick=\"bcv(21,6,12)\">Eccl 6:12</ref>; <ref ref=\"Eccl 7:15\" b=\"21\" cBegin=\"7\" vBegin=\"15\" cEnd=\"7\" vEnd=